 b(0) + c = 5 \\implies c = 5\n     \\]\n\n   - For the point \\((5,0)\\):\n     \\[\n     a(5)^2 + b(5) + c = 0 \\implies 25a + 5b + c = 0\n     \\]\n\n2. **Substitute \\(c = 5\\) into the other equations:**\n\n   - From \\(a - b + c = 0\\):\n     \\[\n     a - b + 5 = 0 \\implies a - b = -5\n     \\]\n\n   - From \\(25a + 5b + c = 0\\):\n     \\[\n     25a + 5b + 5 = 0 \\implies 25a + 5b = -5\n     \\]\n\n3. **Solve the system of linear equations:**\n\n   - We have:\n     \\[\n     a - b = -5 \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     25a + 5b = -5 \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)}\n     \\]\n\n   - Multiply Equation 1 by 5 to align the coefficients of \\(b\\):\n     \\[\n     5a - 5b = -25 \\quad \\text{(Equation 3)}\n     \\]\n\n   - Add Equation 2 and Equation 3:\n     \\[\n     (25a + 5b) + (5a - 5b) = -5 + (-25) \\implies 30a = -30 \\implies a = -1\n     \\]\n\n   - Substitute \\(a = -1\\) back into Equation 1:\n     \\[\n     -1 - b = -5 \\implies -b = -4 \\implies b = 4\n     \\]\n\n4. **Verify the values \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\):**\n\n   - We have \\(a = -1\\), \\(b = 4\\), and \\(c = 5\\).\n\n5. **Calculate \\(100a + 10b + c\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   100a + 10b + c = 100(-1) + 10(4) + 5 = -100 + 40 + 5 = -55\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(100a + 10b + c\\) is \\(\\boxed{-55}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-55}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:75"}
